    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process#ChemicalRecyclingProcess">
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Recycling process using chemical transformation to recover material from textile products or textile waste.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Chemical recycling process</rdfs:label>
        <textile-connector:modellingNote xml:lang="en">This class represents a recycling process type. Product recyclability, barriers, compatibility and recyclability assessment belong to the Textile Recyclability module.</textile-connector:modellingNote>
        <textile-connector:sourceLocator xml:lang="en">JRC Preparatory Study, Section 3.3.1, printed pages 27, 29, lines 536-547; JRC Preparatory Study, Section 3.3.1, Table 8, printed page 27; caption line 546.</textile-connector:sourceLocator>
        <textile-connector:sourceType rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#adaptedDefinition"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process#MechanicalRecyclingProcess">
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Recycling process mechanically transforming textile products or textile waste into reusable fibres or materials.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Mechanical recycling process</rdfs:label>
        <textile-connector:modellingNote xml:lang="en">This class represents a recycling process type. Product recyclability, barriers, compatibility and recyclability assessment belong to the Textile Recyclability module.</textile-connector:modellingNote>
        <textile-connector:sourceLocator xml:lang="en">JRC Preparatory Study, Section 3.3.1, printed pages 27, 29, lines 536-547; JRC Preparatory Study, Section 3.3.1, Table 8, printed page 27; caption line 546.</textile-connector:sourceLocator>
        <textile-connector:sourceType rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#adaptedDefinition"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process#RepairProcess">
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Repair can extend the usable lifetime of a textile product, but this module does not import TEXTILE_INDICATOR. Links from repair to product lifetime indicators should be handled in TEXTILE_INDICATOR or in a cross-module relation layer.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Repair process</rdfs:label>
        <textile-connector:evidenceStatus rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#reconstructedEvidence"/>
        <textile-connector:evidenceStatus rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#supportingEvidence"/>
        <textile-connector:modellingNote xml:lang="en">Repair can extend the usable lifetime of a textile product. Product lifetime indicators are represented in TEXTILE_INDICATOR, and any formal link should be handled there or in a cross-module relation layer.</textile-connector:modellingNote>
        <textile-connector:modellingNote xml:lang="en">This class represents a repair activity or process type. Repairability capability, repair service information and repairability assessment belong to Textile Repairability.</textile-connector:modellingNote>
        <textile-connector:sourceLocator xml:lang="en">JRC Preparatory Study, Section 9.2.3.2, printed page 129, lines 3466-3476; JRC Preparatory Study, Section 9.2.3.3, printed pages 129-130, lines 3477-3484; JRC Preparatory Study, Section 13.10.1.5, printed pages 473-474, lines 11273-11326.</textile-connector:sourceLocator>
        <textile-connector:sourceType rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#adaptedDefinition"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process#TargetFabricDensity">
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A process target specification stating the intended thread or loop density of the resulting fabric.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Target fabric density</rdfs:label>
        <textile-connector:modellingNote xml:lang="en">Fabric density is related to thread count or loop density. Its effects on breathability, handle and appearance are mediated by fabric type and construction.</textile-connector:modellingNote>
        <textile-connector:modellingNote xml:lang="en">The process-side target remains distinct from the resulting characteristic represented in Textile Structure.</textile-connector:modellingNote>
        <textile-connector:modellingNote xml:lang="en">This class is not declared equivalent to txtstr:ThreadCount. FabricDensity is process-side and may cover thread density, loop density or related construction-density settings; ThreadCount is the structure-side fabric characteristic currently represented in TEXTILE_STRUCTURE.</textile-connector:modellingNote>
        <textile-connector:sourceLocator xml:lang="en">JRC Preparatory Study, Section 13.10.2, printed pages 493-495, lines 11902-11920; JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, Table 182, printed page 302; caption line 9114.</textile-connector:sourceLocator>
        <textile-connector:sourceType rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#adaptedDefinition"/>
        <textile-connector:typicalInfluenceOn rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FabricAppearance"/>
        <textile-connector:typicalInfluenceOn rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FabricBreathability"/>
        <textile-connector:typicalInfluenceOn rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FabricHandle"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability#RefurbishmentProcess">
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Process involving preparation, cleaning, testing, servicing and, where necessary, repair to restore a textile product within its originally intended use and performance range.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Refurbishment process</rdfs:label>
        <textile-connector:sourceLocator xml:lang="en">JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, printed pages 15-16, lines 218-222; JRC Preparatory Study, Section 13.10.1.7, printed page 475, lines 11374-11400; JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, Table 2, printed page 15; caption line 219.</textile-connector:sourceLocator>
        <textile-connector:sourceType rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#adaptedDefinition"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability#RemanufacturingProcess">
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Process producing a new textile product from waste objects, products or components, with at least one change that may affect performance, purpose or type. It is distinct from material recycling.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Remanufacturing process</rdfs:label>
        <textile-connector:sourceLocator xml:lang="en">JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, printed pages 16-17, lines 222-225; JRC Preparatory Study, Section 13.10.1.13, printed pages 480-481, lines 11645-11673; JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, Table 2, printed page 15; caption line 219.</textile-connector:sourceLocator>
        <textile-connector:sourceType rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#adaptedDefinition"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability#UpgradeProcess">
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Textile intervention process intended to enhance the functionality, performance, capacity, safety or aesthetics of a product or component.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-repairability"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Upgrade process</rdfs:label>
        <textile-connector:sourceLocator xml:lang="en">JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, printed pages 15-16, lines 218-222; JRC Preparatory Study, Section 9.1.2, printed pages 101-102, lines 2722-2728; JRC Preparatory Study, Section 13.10.1.4, printed page 472, lines 11264-11272; JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, Table 2, printed page 15; caption line 219.</textile-connector:sourceLocator>
        <textile-connector:sourceType rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#adaptedDefinition"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#ThreadCount">
        <terms:source rdf:resource="https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Fabric construction characteristic expressing the number of threads per specified unit length in a woven fabric.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Thread count</rdfs:label>
        <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process#TargetFabricDensity"/>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Number of threads</skos:altLabel>
        <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Thread density</skos:altLabel>
        <textile-connector:evidenceStatus rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#explicitEvidence"/>
        <textile-connector:modellingNote xml:lang="en">Although the JRC uses the term thread count, its definition is a density per unit length. A quantitative value should therefore include a reciprocal-length unit rather than a dimensionless count.</textile-connector:modellingNote>
        <textile-connector:modellingNote xml:lang="en">Thread count is represented in TEXTILE_STRUCTURE as a fabric construction characteristic. The related process-side concept txtprc:TargetFabricDensity remains a fabric manufacturing parameter. The two concepts should not be merged automatically; one describes a product/fabric characteristic, the other a process parameter or target.</textile-connector:modellingNote>
        <textile-connector:sourceLocator xml:lang="en">JRC Preparatory Study, Section 13.10.2, printed pages 493-494, lines 11902-11907; JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, Table 182, printed page 302; caption line 9114.</textile-connector:sourceLocator>
        <textile-connector:sourceType rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#adaptedDefinition"/>
        <textile-connector:typicalInfluenceOn rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FabricBreathability"/>
        <textile-connector:typicalInfluenceOn rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FabricHandle"/>
    </rdf:Description>
    


